Title:- CSV File Handling and Basic Statistics Using Scala

Aim:-
To read a CSV file using Scala and calculate basic statistical values such as mean, minimum, and maximum marks.

Program:-
object Main extends App {

  // CSV data
  val csvData =
    """Name,Marks
      |Amit,78
      |Priya,85
      |Rahul,92
      |Sneha,88
      |Karan,75
      |Jyoti,89
      |Samika,93
      |""".stripMargin

  // Split into lines and skip the header
  val lines = csvData.split("\n").drop(1)

  // Extract the Marks column
  val marks = lines.map(_.split(",")(1).toDouble)

  // Calculate statistics
  val mean = marks.sum / marks.length
  val minimum = marks.min
  val maximum = marks.max

  // Display summary
  println("CSV Statistical Report")
  println("CSV Data: " + csvData)
  println("Mean Marks: " + mean)
  println("Minimum Marks: " + minimum)
  println("Maximum Marks: " + maximum)
}


